{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112979","id":3028562833,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc60hDOR","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112979","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112979.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112979.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112979","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112979/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112979/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112979/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0edca497a148e2857ca480798aaa1e2fa1fe6513","number":112979,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"DRAFT: Add EditorCanvasItemGizmoPlugin for 2D (similar to 3D's Node3DEditorGizmoPlugin) ","user":{"login":"derkork","id":327257,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNzI1Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/327257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork","html_url":"https://github.com/derkork","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derkork/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This adds Gizmo plugins for canvas items similar to what the Spatial Editor Gizmo plugin can do (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1910). This is intended to simplify building editor extensions for 2D objects, which currently has a lot of limitations. \r\n\r\nRight now, this is still a draft. It's nowhere near finished, but I still wanted to put it up here so I could get some early feedback. Just to avoid running into the wrong direction for a long time, and then it's a big mess to clean everything up.\r\n\r\nIf that is not the correct way to do this, please let me know, and I will close this and reopen the merge request once I think it is in a state that I would consider finished. \r\n\r\nMy plan of attack right now is: \r\n\r\n - Implement the functionality of the Gizmo plugins so that add-ons and GD extensions can use them to create their own editor integrations that have a similar level of integration that we currently get with the 3D stuff. \r\n - Follow the style, approach and naming of the existing Node3D editor gizmo system as closely as possible to make it easy for engine developers to maintain both systems because they work in a consistent way. \r\n - I would keep the editors for the existing 2D nodes as they are right now.  I'm hoping that with this approach we can get this feature into the engine quicker and with less risk of breaking mission-critical stuff.\r\n - Eventually, there would be a second pull request that migrates all the existing 2D editors to the new gizmo system and removes the plumbing that is currently used by the 2D editors, like all the `_edit_*` methods. \r\n\r\nWhat is currently working:\r\n\r\n- [x] You can register new canvas item gizmo plugins to GDScript. \r\n- [x] You can draw stuff over nodes. \r\n- [x] You can define picking collision shapes which are used to pick nodes with a single mouse click and rectangle selection.\r\n- [x] You can define handles.\r\n- [x] You can move handles.\r\n- [x] You can define subgizmos.\r\n- [x] You can select subgizmos (single pick and rectangle selection).\r\n- [x] Gizmos can be shown and hidden in the gizmo menu. \r\n- [x] You can define a boundary and a pivot and edit them (equivalent of `_edit_get/set/has_rect`  and `_edit/get/set/has/_pivot`). \r\n- [x] You can transform subgizmos (move/rotate/scale, supports temporary pivots).  \r\n- [x] Undo/redo fully works.\r\n- [x] [Documentation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/11853) and [demo project](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/pull/1305)\r\n\r\nWhat's still missing:\r\n- [ ] Polish, quite a bit of it.   \r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/fo